Here’s the update on yesterday’s MCP hands-on work: 03-09-2026

Integrated the Groq LLM with our MCP client.
Implemented LLM-based tool selection, allowing the model to decide which MCP tool should be used based on the user’s request.
Dynamically converted the MCP tool definitions and input schemas into the format required by Groq.
Implemented the complete LLM → MCP Tool → Tool Result → LLM workflow.
Added support for passing MCP tool results back to the LLM to generate the final response.
Improved tool input validation using structured schemas, including allowed operations for the calculation tool.
Added handling for MCP tool errors so that errors can be returned to the LLM instead of causing the client to fail.
Implemented an initial agent loop that allows the LLM to continue processing until it no longer requests a tool.
Tested the workflow with customer search and calculation queries, including combined requests.

Current status: The basic LLM + MCP agent workflow is working successfully.
Next, I will focus on improving multi-tool execution and making the agent flow.



